      "**Context**",
      "Through our earlier exchanges with companies, we had gradually come to understand that translating a research project into industrial practice involves far more than experimental results. Risks must be systematically identified and managed, products require clearly defined quality control systems, processes must be reproducible, and market positioning must be grounded in actual clinical needs. As these issues became clearer, however, we recognized that understanding industrialization does not mean having entered industry. Our previous exchanges had primarily helped us reassess CirCure from a company’s perspective. The next questions were more direct: when we present the project to industry, what do companies actually expect to see? What is CirCure currently missing? Is there scope for further dialogue and collaboration? We therefore held further project discussions with Jilin Jika Biotechnology Co., Ltd. and Jilin Province Ji’en Zhihe Biotherapeutic Technology Co., Ltd. For us, this was also an important attempt to move our Entrepreneurship work from industry consultation toward industry engagement.",
